    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Why Modern Businesses Need Smarter Financial Management
        </h2>

        <p>
            Managing business finances involves much more than recording
            transactions. Companies must monitor income and expenses, reconcile
            bank statements, manage accounts payable and receivable, and prepare
            reliable financial reports. When these activities depend on
            spreadsheets and disconnected applications, financial management
            becomes time-consuming and more vulnerable to errors.
        </p>

        <p>
            As businesses grow, the volume and complexity of financial
            transactions increase. Finance teams need accurate information,
            consistent processes, and timely reporting to maintain control over
            cash flow and support strategic decisions. Manual workflows can make
            it difficult to obtain a complete picture of the company's financial
            position.
        </p>

        <p>
            Odoo Accounting brings essential accounting activities into an
            integrated business platform. By connecting financial records with
            sales, purchasing, invoicing, and other operations, businesses can
            reduce repetitive work and improve visibility across their financial
            processes.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            What Makes Odoo Accounting Different?
        </h2>

        <p>
            Odoo Accounting combines core accounting capabilities with the wider
            Odoo business ecosystem. Instead of managing financial information
            in isolated systems, companies can connect accounting workflows with
            operational activities that generate financial transactions.
        </p>

        <p>
            For example, a confirmed sales order can lead to an invoice, while
            supplier bills can be managed alongside purchasing activities.
            Depending on the configuration, these transactions can generate
            accounting entries that help maintain consistent financial records.
        </p>

        <p>
            This integrated approach reduces unnecessary duplication and gives
            authorized users a more connected view of business activity. The
            specific capabilities available depend on the Odoo version,
            installed applications, accounting localization, and configuration.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Automate Everyday Accounting Tasks
        </h2>

        <p>
            Routine accounting activities can consume a significant amount of
            time. Recording transactions, processing invoices, categorizing
            expenses, and updating financial records are necessary tasks, but
            performing each step manually can limit the time available for
            analysis and planning.
        </p>

        <p>
            Odoo Accounting supports workflows that reduce manual data entry and
            connect financial transactions with their corresponding business
            documents. Automated accounting entries, configurable processes, and
            integrated invoicing can help teams manage recurring activities more
            consistently.
        </p>

        <p>
            Automation is most effective when supported by clear accounting
            policies and appropriate controls. Businesses should define approval
            responsibilities, review transaction rules, and establish procedures
            for handling exceptions before relying on automated workflows.
        </p>
    </section>

